# Compose UI Conventions

## Placement
- Put reusable UI in `shared/src/commonMain/...` (theme, components, screens).
- Keep platform entry points thin (`androidApp`, `iosApp`, `webApp`, `desktopApp`).

## Style
- Match shop.app look: light gray backgrounds, white surfaces, strong purple accent, large corner radii, generous spacing.
- Prefer shared building blocks (`SearchBar`, `ProductCard`, `SectionHeader`, nav) over one-off copies.
- Use `Arrangement.Start` / `End` (not raw Left/Right) so RTL mirrors correctly.

## Scope
- One component or one section per change unless the user asks for more.
- No networking, repositories with real HTTP, or purchase screens in this phase.

## When to use
- When editing or creating Kotlin/Compose files.

## When to update
- Package/folder layout becomes stable or changes.
- Shared component naming conventions settle.
- Repeated UI mistakes appear (wrong radius, LTR-only layout, duplicated cards).
